Topic: Why Problem-Solving Matters in Software Engineering

Problem-solving is one of the most important skills for a software engineer because programming is not only about writing code. A developer first needs to understand the problem, identify the requirements, and determine the best approach. Sometimes the simplest solution is enough, while in other situations an optimized algorithm is necessary. Good problem-solving also helps during debugging. Instead of changing code randomly, an engineer should identify the root cause and then test possible solutions systematically. I also believe communication is part of problem-solving because a good solution needs to be explained clearly to teammates. During interviews, I try to explain my thought process before writing the final code. This shows that I understand not only how to implement a solution but also why I chose that particular approach. Developing this skill through regular practice will help me both in technical interviews and in real software projects.

